# ADR-0452 item 8, INV-0453-1, INV-0453-2, INV-0454-2: Rust's std as a POSIX program (tests/rust-std/, built by
# tools/zcargo), through the broker under its description, on the normal kernel. run by `make test-rust-std`,
# which turns @PORT@ and @HOST@ into the test server's.
! ZORAYA-PANIC
! first process ended
! FAIL
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
# The lease takes a few hundred milliseconds under TCG.
> sleep 3\r
< \r\n~>
> rstest hello\r
< hello from Rust std
< rstest: hello passed
< \r\n~>
> rstest syscall\r
< rstest: syscall passed
< \r\n~>
> rstest time\r
< rstest: time passed
< \r\n~>
> rstest hash\r
< rstest: hash passed
< \r\n~>
> rstest threads\r
< rstest: threads passed
< \r\n~>
# std::fs: the program's own /tmp, and a directory the line grants; one the line does not grant is not found.
> rstest fs /tmp\r
< rstest: fs passed
< \r\n~>
> +w /work/granted rstest fs /work/granted\r
< rstest: fs passed
< \r\n~>
> rstest denied /work/secret\r
< rstest: denied passed
< hint: rstest tried to
< \r\n~>
# std::process::Command: both ways of starting a child; each child hashes (its own random connection) and has no
# network; uid and gid fail and the child never runs.
> rstest process\r
< rstest: process passed
< \r\n~>
# Panics unwind through the sysroot's libunwind; an uncaught one ends with 101, abort with signal 6, an overflow is a fault.
> rstest panic\r
< rstest: panic passed
< \r\n~>
> rstest uncaught\r
< nobody catches this
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< exit status 101
< \r\n~>
> rstest abort\r
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< signal 6
< \r\n~>
> rstest overflow\r
< \r\n~>
> status\r
< data abort
< \r\n~>
# std::net under the grant of the line: by address and by name, a non-blocking connect, another port refused.
> rsnet http://@HOST@:@PORT@/pattern/300000\r
< rstest: net passed
< \r\n~>
> +net test.zoraya:@PORT@ rsnet http://test.zoraya:@PORT@/pattern/300000\r
< rstest: net passed
< \r\n~>
> poweroff\r
